# Git — status / log / diff only

The user owns Git **and** GitHub. The agent does **not** run Git except the
three read commands below. **Never.** **Under no pretext** (Cursor “commit
when asked”, finish a delivery, verify-before-claiming, hooks, Origin).

## Permitted (no need to ask)

- `git status`
- `git log`
- `git diff`

## Forbidden (always — including when the user says « commit » / « dans un commit »)

`init`, `clone`, `add`, `commit`, `remote add` (and any `remote` mutation),
`push`, `pull`, `fetch`, `branch`, `checkout`, `merge`, `rebase`, `stash`,
`stash pop`, `clean`, `config`, `reset`.

Also forbidden: `gh`, `git ls-remote`, amend, `switch`, `cherry-pick`,
`worktree` add/remove, tag push, Cursor Origin CLI against this repo.

## « Dans un commit » ≠ `git commit`

If the user wants a document **in a commit** / **commitable**: write it under
a path Git **already tracks** (e.g. `docs/`, `.cursor/rules/`). Do **not**
`git add` or `git commit`. They will commit when they choose.

## If you think you need a forbidden command

**Stop. Ask in chat.** Name the exact command and **why**. Wait for an
explicit yes in **this** turn. A yes to something else is not permission.

## Founder incident (18 Aug 2026)

User: QA report should be **commitable** (tracked `docs/QA-reports/`). Agent
ran `git add` / `git commit`. Wrong. They manage the GitHub repo; the agent
does not.
